# Travis Picking with a Melody (repertoire plan: st-travis-melody). An original 16-bar tune in
# C major over C, F, G7 and Am, in four 4-bar phrases:
#   C C F C | Am Am G7 G7 | F C F G7 | C Am G7 C.
# The thumb (P) keeps the alternating bass of the Travis Picking study on every beat, lightly
# palm muted: C (x32010) string 5 fret 3, string 4 fret 2, string 6 fret 3, string 4 fret 2;
# Am (x02210) string 5 open, string 4 fret 2; G7 (320001) string 6 fret 3, string 4 open;
# F (xx3211) string 4 fret 3, string 3 fret 2.
# The tune is on strings 1 and 2 only: m plucks string 1, i plucks string 2. A tune note on a beat
# is pinched with the thumb; a tune note on an "and" falls between two thumb notes (syncopated).
# At the ends of bars 4 and 8 the tune arrives half a beat early, on the "and" of 4, and rings into
# the next bar while the thumb carries on. D on string 2 fret 3 and G on string 1 fret 3 are
# played by finger 4 on top of the chord shape; B is string 2 open (lift finger 1).
title: Travis Picking with a Melody
composer: Sixstring Academy
source: Original fingerstyle study
licence: Original study for Sixstring Academy
difficulty: 5
tags: travis picking, alternating bass, fingerstyle, melody, syncopation, pinch
tempo: 80
time: 4/4
key: C

track: Your part
role: lead
[Phrase 1]
| "C=x32010" q (5:3{P 3 pm} 1:0{M}) e 4:2{P 2 pm} 1:3{M 4} q 6:3{P 3 pm} (4:2{P pm} 1:0{M}) | q (5:3{P pm} 2:3{I 4}) (4:2{P pm} 2:1{I 1}) 6:3{P pm} 4:2{P pm} |
| "F=xx3211" q (4:3{P 3 pm} 1:1{M 1}) e 3:2{P 2 pm} 1:3{M 4} q 4:3{P pm} (3:2{P pm} 1:1{M}) | "C" q (5:3{pm} 1:0{M}) 4:2{pm} 6:3{pm} ^"tune arrives early" e 4:2{pm} 2:1{I 1} |
[Phrase 2]
| "Am=x02210" q 5:0{pm} e 4:2{pm} 1:0{M} q 5:0{pm} (4:2{pm} 2:3{I 4}) | q (5:0{pm} 2:1{I 1}) (4:2{pm} 2:0{I}) 5:0{pm} 4:2{pm} |
| "G7=320001" q (6:3{3 pm} 2:3{I 4}) e 4:0{pm} 1:1{M 1} q 6:3{pm} (4:0{pm} 2:3{I 4}) | q (6:3{pm} 2:0{I}) 4:0{pm} 6:3{pm} e 4:0{pm} 2:1{I 1} |
[Phrase 3]
| "F" q 4:3{3 pm} e 3:2{2 pm} 1:1{M 1} q 4:3{pm} (3:2{pm} 1:3{M 4}) | "C" q (5:3{3 pm} 1:0{M}) (4:2{pm} 2:3{I 4}) (6:3{3 pm} 2:1{I 1}) 4:2{pm} |
| "F" q (4:3{pm} 1:1{M}) e 3:2{pm} 1:3{M 4} q 4:3{pm} (3:2{pm} 1:1{M}) | "G7" q (6:3{pm} 1:3{M 4}) e 4:0{pm} 1:1{M 1} q 6:3{pm} (4:0{pm} 2:3{I 4}) |
